COMMANDS RUN:
 - Bash: cat .git-blame-ignore-revs; git ls-files | sed 's|/.*||' | sort | uniq -c | sort -rn | head -20; git log --format='%h %an <%ae> %s' | head -20; git shortlog -sne | head -20
 - Bash: cat /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-efe-claude-kredi-runs-2026-10-23-r11-f9-claude-opus-5-5-E-runs-HE2-bf-1-repo/14b2f455-aae7-4d6c-b73d-3066c33f202d/tasks/by2f0eyk5.output
 - Bash: git shortlog -sne HEAD </dev/null | head; head -5 attribute_string.go; wc -l *.go; git ls-files vendor | head; git show --stat dee565e | tail -5
blame(){ for f in $(git ls-files '*.go' ':!vendor' ':!attribute_string.go'); do git blame --line-porcelain $@ HEAD -- "$f" | sed -n 's/^author //p'; done | sort | uniq -c | sort -rn; }
echo "== raw"; blame
echo "== ignore-revs + -w -C -C -M"; blame -w -M -C -C --ignore-revs-file .git-blame-ignore-revs
 - Bash: ls .mailmap 2>&1; for f in $(git ls-files '*.go' ':!vendor' ':!attribute_string.go'); do git blame --line-porcelain -w -M -C -C --ignore-revs-file .git-blame-ignore-revs HEAD -- "$f" | sed -n 's/^author-mail //p'; done | sort | uniq -c | sort -rn | head -8; git log -1 --format=%ad --date=short --author=Fatih HEAD; git log --format='%an' --since=2025-10-23 HEAD | sort | uniq -c
FINAL ANSWER:
The background command that was just reported as stopped was my first exploratory call. Its last step, `git shortlog` without `HEAD`, hung waiting for input, so it ran until the time limit and was stopped. I then ran that step again correctly (with `HEAD`) in a later command. The ownership numbers in my previous answer come from those later runs and are unchanged.
